 "id": "321-49",
 "split": "screen_long",
 "sentences": [
  "For Python coding, always add the '@rename_kwargs' decorator from the 'pedantic' module to all methods.",
  "This helps us maintain clean and readable code.",
  "It's important to maintain consistency across our codebases to make collaboration easier.",
  "By committing directly, your changes will be immediately visible to the entire team.",
  "It fosters a more collaborative environment, as everyone can see and discuss the latest developments.",
  "First and foremost, make sure your code is well-tested before committing.",
  "Also, remember to include clear and concise commit messages.",
  "Document your changes properly so that other team members can easily understand your work.",
  "Yes, for this project, I want you to emphasize unit testing.",
  "Write comprehensive test cases that cover all the functions and modules you're working on.",
  "Our goal is to achieve high test coverage, ensuring that any changes or additions are thoroughly validated.",
  "Don't hesitate to reach out to your colleagues if you need help or if you want to discuss testing strategies.",
  "Collaboration is key, and your teammates will be happy to help.",
  "One important practice is to keep your commits atomic.",
  "That is, each commit should represent a single, logical change.",
  "This makes it easier for others to understand and review your changes.",
  "Also, don't forget to regularly pull the latest changes from the dev branch to stay up-to-date with your colleagues' work."
 ],
